CORE
main.cpp
--cpp20 --object-bits 11 --no-unwinding-assertions
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ mutable lambda keeps per-object capture state: SUCCESS$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
[expr.prim.lambda.closure]: a mutable lambda's operator() is non-const and its
by-copy captures are mutable non-static data members, so modifications persist
in the closure object across calls.  Lambda rework Phase D lowers a mutable
lambda to a closure whose operator() is non-const, so the captured counter
persists per closure object.
